1
00:00:00,182 --> 00:00:02,984
Linear functions are
everywhere on the SAT,

2
00:00:03,004 --> 00:00:05,861
and a lot of them come wrapped in a story.

3
00:00:06,218 --> 00:00:07,340
A gym membership.

4
00:00:07,360 --> 00:00:08,948
A tank filling with water.

5
00:00:08,968 --> 00:00:09,912
A savings account.

6
00:00:09,932 --> 00:00:11,341
The math is easy.

7
00:00:11,361 --> 00:00:14,147
The hard part is reading
what the numbers mean.

8
00:00:14,232 --> 00:00:18,605
The most common mistakes are mixing
up the slope and the intercept,

9
00:00:18,625 --> 00:00:21,711
and describing the slope
with the wrong units.

10
00:00:21,731 --> 00:00:25,446
Interpretation questions are
built to catch exactly that.

11
00:00:25,483 --> 00:00:29,749
In this video: slope as a rate,
the intercept as a starting value,

12
00:00:29,769 --> 00:00:33,855
how to interpret any coefficient, how
to build an equation from words or a

13
00:00:33,875 --> 00:00:37,069
table, and inequalities in context.

14
00:00:37,089 --> 00:00:40,304
Six practice questions, from easy to hard.

15
00:00:40,379 --> 00:00:43,895
Every linear function looks
like y equals m x plus b.

16
00:00:43,915 --> 00:00:47,145
In a word problem,
those letters have jobs.

17
00:00:47,165 --> 00:00:51,573
m is the rate: how much y changes
for each one unit increase in x.

18
00:00:51,593 --> 00:00:55,415
b is the starting value:
what y is when x is zero.

19
00:00:55,463 --> 00:00:56,550
Here's an example.

20
00:00:56,570 --> 00:01:01,657
A gym charges a forty dollar sign-up
fee plus twenty-five dollars per month.

21
00:01:01,677 --> 00:01:06,228
The total cost is C equals
twenty-five m plus forty,

22
00:01:06,248 --> 00:01:08,355
where m is the number of months.

23
00:01:08,383 --> 00:01:09,649
Twenty-five is the slope.

24
00:01:09,669 --> 00:01:13,578
Its units are dollars per month, so the
cost goes up twenty-five dollars for

25
00:01:13,598 --> 00:01:14,292
each month.

26
00:01:14,312 --> 00:01:16,149
Forty is the intercept.

27
00:01:16,169 --> 00:01:20,041
When m is zero, before any
months, you've paid forty dollars.

28
00:01:20,061 --> 00:01:21,455
That's the sign-up fee.

29
00:01:21,481 --> 00:01:24,194
Use these two sentences
for any linear model.

30
00:01:24,837 --> 00:01:28,532
For a slope: for each
one unit increase in x,

31
00:01:28,552 --> 00:01:30,104
y changes by the slope.

32
00:01:30,124 --> 00:01:32,531
If the slope is negative, y goes down.

33
00:01:32,551 --> 00:01:35,731
For an intercept: when x is
zero, y equals the intercept.

34
00:01:36,192 --> 00:01:38,886
The SAT tests this in three main ways.

35
00:01:38,906 --> 00:01:43,029
First, interpretation: what does
this number mean in context?

36
00:01:43,049 --> 00:01:47,906
Second, building: write the equation
from a description or a table.

37
00:01:48,049 --> 00:01:51,422
Third, inequalities: at most, at least,

38
00:01:51,442 --> 00:01:53,295
and which values are possible.

39
00:01:53,315 --> 00:01:55,581
Interpretation questions come up a lot,

40
00:01:55,601 --> 00:01:57,601
and they usually look like this.

41
00:01:57,672 --> 00:02:01,795
What is the best interpretation
of twelve in this context?

42
00:02:01,815 --> 00:02:04,008
Every answer choice sounds reasonable,

43
00:02:04,028 --> 00:02:06,994
so you have to test each
one against the equation.

44
00:02:07,048 --> 00:02:07,814
Question one.

45
00:02:07,834 --> 00:02:13,135
The equation V equals twelve t plus
one hundred fifty gives the volume V,

46
00:02:13,155 --> 00:02:19,243
in gallons, of water in a tank t minutes
after a pump starts filling the tank.

47
00:02:19,263 --> 00:02:23,048
What is the best interpretation
of twelve in this context?

48
00:02:23,078 --> 00:02:24,685
Pause and try it.

49
00:02:27,908 --> 00:02:31,244
Twelve is the coefficient
of t, so it's the slope,

50
00:02:31,264 --> 00:02:32,888
and slope is a rate.

51
00:02:32,908 --> 00:02:35,530
Its units are the y units per x unit:

52
00:02:35,550 --> 00:02:36,837
gallons per minute.

53
00:02:36,872 --> 00:02:40,459
So each minute, the volume
goes up by twelve gallons.

54
00:02:40,479 --> 00:02:41,872
The answer is B.

55
00:02:41,904 --> 00:02:42,813
Test the others.

56
00:02:42,833 --> 00:02:45,706
A says the tank started
with twelve gallons.

57
00:02:45,726 --> 00:02:48,634
But the starting amount
is V when t is zero,

58
00:02:48,654 --> 00:02:50,276
which is one hundred fifty.

59
00:02:50,296 --> 00:02:52,955
D says twelve gallons after one minute,

60
00:02:52,975 --> 00:02:56,118
but V of one is one hundred sixty-two.

61
00:02:56,476 --> 00:02:58,512
And C is wrong too.

62
00:02:58,547 --> 00:03:01,884
Adding one hundred fifty gallons
takes twelve and a half minutes,

63
00:03:01,904 --> 00:03:02,899
not twelve.

64
00:03:02,919 --> 00:03:03,935
Question two.

65
00:03:03,955 --> 00:03:08,863
A hiker's distance d, in miles, from the
end of a trail h hours after she starts

66
00:03:08,883 --> 00:03:13,649
hiking is given by d equals
fourteen minus two point five h.

67
00:03:13,669 --> 00:03:17,419
What is the best interpretation
of fourteen in this context?

68
00:03:17,473 --> 00:03:19,080
Pause and try it.

69
00:03:22,303 --> 00:03:26,319
Fourteen is the constant, so it's
the value of d when h is zero.

70
00:03:26,339 --> 00:03:30,247
At the moment she starts hiking, she's
fourteen miles from the end of the trail.

71
00:03:30,267 --> 00:03:31,840
The answer is C.

72
00:03:31,860 --> 00:03:33,126
Two point five is the rate.

73
00:03:33,146 --> 00:03:36,376
She gets two point five
miles closer every hour.

74
00:03:36,396 --> 00:03:39,554
So A, which calls fourteen her speed,

75
00:03:39,574 --> 00:03:41,090
is wrong, and so is B.

76
00:03:41,110 --> 00:03:44,304
She covers two point five
miles in the first hour,

77
00:03:44,324 --> 00:03:45,610
not fourteen.

78
00:03:45,646 --> 00:03:46,947
D is wrong too.

79
00:03:46,967 --> 00:03:50,824
Fourteen divided by two point
five is five point six hours.

80
00:03:50,865 --> 00:03:52,345
Question three.

81
00:03:52,365 --> 00:03:56,381
A student deposits the same amount
into a savings account each week.

82
00:03:56,401 --> 00:03:59,631
The table shows the amount A, in dollars,

83
00:03:59,651 --> 00:04:03,452
in the account w weeks after the
student started making deposits.

84
00:04:03,472 --> 00:04:06,024
At two weeks, it's three
hundred forty dollars.

85
00:04:06,044 --> 00:04:08,425
At five weeks, four hundred forty-five.

86
00:04:08,445 --> 00:04:11,194
At nine weeks, five hundred eighty-five.

87
00:04:11,231 --> 00:04:13,546
Which equation represents
this relationship?

88
00:04:13,566 --> 00:04:15,174
Pause and try it.

89
00:04:19,397 --> 00:04:21,289
Find the slope first.

90
00:04:21,467 --> 00:04:25,948
From week two to week five, the amount
goes from three hundred forty to four

91
00:04:25,968 --> 00:04:27,289
hundred forty-five.

92
00:04:27,325 --> 00:04:30,019
That's one hundred five
dollars over three weeks,

93
00:04:30,039 --> 00:04:32,022
or thirty-five dollars per week.

94
00:04:32,042 --> 00:04:33,236
Now the intercept.

95
00:04:33,256 --> 00:04:35,558
Work back from week two to week zero.

96
00:04:35,578 --> 00:04:38,094
Two weeks at thirty-five
dollars is seventy,

97
00:04:38,114 --> 00:04:41,558
and three hundred forty minus
seventy is two hundred seventy.

98
00:04:41,578 --> 00:04:46,040
So A equals thirty-five w
plus two hundred seventy.

99
00:04:46,060 --> 00:04:47,739
The answer is A.

100
00:04:47,917 --> 00:04:52,683
Check week nine: thirty-five times
nine is three hundred fifteen,

101
00:04:52,703 --> 00:04:56,202
plus two hundred seventy is
five hundred eighty-five.

102
00:04:56,356 --> 00:04:57,764
B is the big trap.

103
00:04:57,784 --> 00:05:00,872
It uses three hundred forty
as the starting value,

104
00:05:00,892 --> 00:05:04,176
but that's the amount at
week two, not week zero.

105
00:05:04,249 --> 00:05:06,943
C uses one hundred five,
the change in dollars,

106
00:05:06,963 --> 00:05:08,872
without dividing by the change in weeks.

107
00:05:08,892 --> 00:05:11,570
It fits the first row and nothing else.

108
00:05:11,649 --> 00:05:12,970
Desmos shortcut.

109
00:05:13,113 --> 00:05:18,200
Add a table and enter the weeks
as x one and the dollars as y one.

110
00:05:18,220 --> 00:05:22,683
Then type y one, tilde, m x one plus b.

111
00:05:22,899 --> 00:05:27,780
Desmos returns m equals thirty-five
and b equals two hundred seventy.

112
00:05:27,800 --> 00:05:28,994
Question four.

113
00:05:29,014 --> 00:05:33,514
A plumber charges a fixed fee
for each job plus an hourly rate.

114
00:05:33,764 --> 00:05:36,637
A two hour job costs one
hundred ninety dollars,

115
00:05:36,657 --> 00:05:40,514
and a five hour job costs three
hundred eighty-five dollars.

116
00:05:40,907 --> 00:05:43,867
What is the plumber's
fixed fee, in dollars?

117
00:05:43,887 --> 00:05:45,494
Pause and try it.

118
00:05:48,718 --> 00:05:50,233
Treat each job as a point.

119
00:05:50,253 --> 00:05:52,733
Two hours and one hundred ninety dollars.

120
00:05:52,753 --> 00:05:55,610
Five hours and three
hundred eighty-five dollars.

121
00:05:55,859 --> 00:05:57,768
The hourly rate is the slope.

122
00:05:57,788 --> 00:06:01,876
The cost goes up one hundred ninety-five
dollars over three extra hours.

123
00:06:01,896 --> 00:06:04,610
That's sixty-five dollars per hour.

124
00:06:04,641 --> 00:06:07,478
The fixed fee is the cost at zero hours,

125
00:06:07,498 --> 00:06:08,676
the intercept.

126
00:06:09,141 --> 00:06:12,835
A two hour job includes two
hours at sixty-five dollars,

127
00:06:12,855 --> 00:06:14,549
which is one hundred thirty.

128
00:06:14,569 --> 00:06:17,799
One hundred ninety minus
one hundred thirty is sixty.

129
00:06:17,819 --> 00:06:20,141
The fixed fee is sixty dollars.

130
00:06:20,163 --> 00:06:21,429
Check with the other job.

131
00:06:21,449 --> 00:06:26,393
Sixty plus five times sixty-five is
sixty plus three hundred twenty-five,

132
00:06:26,413 --> 00:06:27,856
which is three hundred eighty-five.

133
00:06:27,876 --> 00:06:32,750
The common mistake is dividing one hundred
ninety by two and calling ninety-five

134
00:06:32,770 --> 00:06:33,714
the hourly rate.

135
00:06:33,734 --> 00:06:35,334
That ignores the fee.

136
00:06:35,354 --> 00:06:36,854
Now inequalities.

137
00:06:37,176 --> 00:06:40,584
Watch for phrases like
at most, no more than,

138
00:06:40,604 --> 00:06:42,961
at least, and a minimum of.

139
00:06:43,212 --> 00:06:46,156
At most and no more than
mean less than or equal to.

140
00:06:46,176 --> 00:06:53,212
At least and a minimum of
mean greater than or equal to.

141
00:06:53,253 --> 00:06:54,447
Question five.

142
00:06:54,467 --> 00:06:57,625
A delivery van can carry at most
one thousand five hundred pounds,

143
00:06:57,645 --> 00:06:59,145
including the driver.

144
00:06:59,324 --> 00:07:01,553
The driver weighs one
hundred eighty pounds,

145
00:07:01,573 --> 00:07:04,287
and each box weighs forty-five pounds.

146
00:07:04,360 --> 00:07:07,840
What is the greatest number of boxes
the van can carry on one trip with the

147
00:07:07,860 --> 00:07:08,624
driver?

148
00:07:08,644 --> 00:07:10,251
Pause and try it.

149
00:07:13,474 --> 00:07:14,903
Build it like an equation.

150
00:07:15,260 --> 00:07:18,097
The driver, plus
forty-five pounds per box,

151
00:07:18,117 --> 00:07:20,739
has to be at most one
thousand five hundred.

152
00:07:20,759 --> 00:07:25,311
So one hundred eighty plus forty-five
b is less than or equal to one thousand

153
00:07:25,331 --> 00:07:26,436
five hundred.

154
00:07:26,456 --> 00:07:31,829
Subtract one hundred eighty, and
forty-five b is at most one thousand three

155
00:07:31,849 --> 00:07:32,472
hundred twenty.

156
00:07:32,492 --> 00:07:37,435
Divide by forty-five, and b is at
most about twenty-nine point three.

157
00:07:37,455 --> 00:07:42,170
You can't load part of a box, and thirty
boxes would put the van over the limit.

158
00:07:42,242 --> 00:07:45,563
The answer is twenty-nine, choice A.

159
00:07:45,606 --> 00:07:47,335
Thirty is the rounding trap.

160
00:07:47,355 --> 00:07:50,999
Thirty-three and thirty-four
come from forgetting the driver.

161
00:07:51,070 --> 00:07:55,372
In Desmos, graph y equals one
hundred eighty plus forty-five x,

162
00:07:55,392 --> 00:07:58,355
and y equals one thousand five hundred.

163
00:07:58,391 --> 00:08:02,461
Zoom out and click the intersection:
about twenty-nine point three.

164
00:08:02,481 --> 00:08:05,124
Twenty-nine is the last
whole number that fits.

165
00:08:05,156 --> 00:08:07,477
Question six, the hardest one.

166
00:08:07,584 --> 00:08:13,422
The function F of h equals forty-eight
minus one point five h gives the amount

167
00:08:13,442 --> 00:08:18,458
of fuel, in liters, in a generator's
tank h hours after the generator starts

168
00:08:18,478 --> 00:08:19,208
running.

169
00:08:19,228 --> 00:08:20,870
Which statement is true?

170
00:08:20,897 --> 00:08:21,627
A.

171
00:08:21,647 --> 00:08:25,540
The fuel decreases by one point
five liters every forty minutes.

172
00:08:25,683 --> 00:08:26,270
B.

173
00:08:26,290 --> 00:08:29,505
It decreases by one liter
every ninety minutes.

174
00:08:29,683 --> 00:08:30,270
C.

175
00:08:30,290 --> 00:08:33,005
The tank runs out after forty-eight hours.

176
00:08:33,112 --> 00:08:33,699
D.

177
00:08:33,719 --> 00:08:36,969
The fuel decreases by one
liter every forty minutes.

178
00:08:37,003 --> 00:08:37,769
Pause and try it.

179
00:08:37,789 --> 00:08:39,288
Take a little longer on this one.

180
00:08:43,525 --> 00:08:45,504
The slope is negative one point five,

181
00:08:45,524 --> 00:08:48,811
so the tank loses one point
five liters every hour.

182
00:08:49,061 --> 00:08:51,147
None of the choices say that directly.

183
00:08:51,167 --> 00:08:53,719
They restate the same
rate in different units.

184
00:08:53,739 --> 00:08:54,811
So convert.

185
00:08:54,832 --> 00:08:57,152
How long does it take to use one liter?

186
00:08:57,259 --> 00:09:00,919
One divided by one point five
is two thirds of an hour.

187
00:09:00,939 --> 00:09:03,562
Two thirds of sixty
minutes is forty minutes.

188
00:09:03,582 --> 00:09:06,561
So the tank loses one
liter every forty minutes.

189
00:09:06,581 --> 00:09:08,381
The answer is D.

190
00:09:08,401 --> 00:09:09,523
A is the trap.

191
00:09:09,543 --> 00:09:12,166
It keeps one point five
liters but shortens the time,

192
00:09:12,186 --> 00:09:13,936
which makes the rate faster.

193
00:09:14,043 --> 00:09:17,523
B mixes up one point five
hours, which is ninety minutes,

194
00:09:17,543 --> 00:09:18,344
with the rate.

195
00:09:18,364 --> 00:09:21,881
And C treats forty-eight as a
time, but it's the starting fuel.

196
00:09:21,901 --> 00:09:24,615
The tank runs out after thirty-two hours.

197
00:09:24,673 --> 00:09:28,724
For any rate in new units, convert every
choice back to the original units and

198
00:09:28,744 --> 00:09:29,438
compare.

199
00:09:29,458 --> 00:09:33,580
One liter every forty minutes is
one liter per two thirds of an hour.

200
00:09:33,600 --> 00:09:35,831
That's one point five liters per hour.

201
00:09:35,851 --> 00:09:36,994
It matches.

202
00:09:37,076 --> 00:09:40,183
Here's the test-day method
for linear word problems.

203
00:09:40,326 --> 00:09:42,683
Step one: label the units.

204
00:09:42,790 --> 00:09:46,198
Write what x and y measure,
like hours and liters.

205
00:09:46,218 --> 00:09:49,933
The slope's units are
always y units per x unit.

206
00:09:50,014 --> 00:09:52,529
Step two: for an interpretation question,

207
00:09:52,549 --> 00:09:54,994
put the number into one
of the two sentences.

208
00:09:55,014 --> 00:09:59,387
For a slope: for each one more
x, y changes by this much.

209
00:09:59,407 --> 00:10:02,708
For an intercept: when
x is zero, y is this.

210
00:10:02,728 --> 00:10:05,226
Then find the choice
that says the same thing.

211
00:10:05,246 --> 00:10:09,834
Step three: for building questions,
get the rate from two points first,

212
00:10:09,854 --> 00:10:12,318
then work back to the value at zero.

213
00:10:12,603 --> 00:10:16,655
For inequalities, translate at
most and at least carefully,

214
00:10:16,675 --> 00:10:19,568
and check whether the answer
has to be a whole number.

215
00:10:19,617 --> 00:10:20,617
Recap.

216
00:10:20,724 --> 00:10:23,724
Slope is a rate, in y units per x unit.

217
00:10:23,831 --> 00:10:27,275
The intercept is the starting
value, when x is zero.

218
00:10:27,295 --> 00:10:30,438
Find the rate from two
points before anything else.

219
00:10:30,473 --> 00:10:33,417
Convert rates that are
restated in new units.

220
00:10:33,437 --> 00:10:37,143
And round inequality answers in
the direction that keeps them true.

221
00:10:37,163 --> 00:10:42,143
Every question here was written for this
video in the style of the real test.

222
00:10:42,163 --> 00:10:46,642
For official practice, the College Board's
free Question Bank lets you filter by

223
00:10:46,662 --> 00:10:49,199
skill, including linear functions.

224
00:10:49,270 --> 00:10:51,020
If this helped, subscribe.

225
00:10:51,199 --> 00:10:53,786
The next video switches
to Reading and Writing:

226
00:10:53,806 --> 00:10:57,520
rhetorical synthesis, the questions
built from a student's notes.
